    "story.fullLead": "Yueyu Detecting is not a one-shot launch. It is a repeatable routine: leave readable sound and text, check with real speakers, then feed the archive back into recognition.",
    "story.fullP1": "In practice we start from material we can truly hear and read: curated Yue opera clips, Qing tanci woodblock pages, and radio-speech threads. Public entries carry short plot intros and multilingual text so first-time visitors can follow along.",
    "story.fullP2": "Recognition is still a baseline demo—Mandarin engines and general models miss and mishear. The point is not to pretend perfection, but to make the loop public: hear → read → correct → feed back. Clearer archives give Speak a chance to move toward living Yueyu and Wu speech.",
